Z||000000||stingant0||12-24-2001||01:34 PM||||My car does not run. I'm getting spark, fuel, and compression. I replaced the computer with one from another fiero I have...nothing. I replaced the distrbutor...nothing. I retimed it nothing. What the heck!!! Timing + Spark + Fuel = fire||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroMaster88||12-24-2001||03:02 PM||||Are your valves moving?  Look inside the oil cap while you have someone crank the engine.  If there is no movement in there, you have a bad timing chain/gear!<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieromaster88sig.gif">  <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>Not your ordinary 88 coupe!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||12-24-2001||03:34 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by stingant0:<BR><B>Timing + Spark + Fuel = fire</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You forgot compression.<BR>Bad timing chain, stuck valve, blown head gasket, even a clogged catalytic will cause the engine not to run.<P>Also too much fuel or air will cause it not to run.<P><BR>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">            <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 12-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Kasdan||12-24-2001||06:50 PM||||"I'm getting spark, fuel, and compression"  No Oreif, he didnt forget compression  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan, 1986 GT<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kassig2.gif">                  <BR>Aftermarket Power Steering, Rebuilt 2.8<BR>http://www.geocities.com/mtyler14/index.html||||reg||1
