Z||000016||Turbo88||12-30-2001||06:31 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by stingant0:<BR><B>the firing oder is right, replaced the map, the ignition module, and they are new plugs and wires. Battery is charged, it cranks and cranks. Fuel pressure at 40 psi, compression at 1-100 2--120--3-121--4-119--5-125--6-123</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Are the plugs wet after you crank it for a bit? If your distrubtor rotor turning when you crank it? (just pull off the cap and have someone crank the engine). ||||reg||1
